

# 💳 Payment Gateway Integration with Stripe/PayPal & Cloudinary

## 🧠 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to integrate **secure online payments** into a web application using **Stripe** or **PayPal**.
It also includes **Cloudinary integration** for managing product images and uploading payment receipts or invoices.

The project is built using **Next.js (frontend)** and **Node.js + Express (backend)**, with **MongoDB** for data storage.

---

## 🚀 Features

✅ Secure payment processing using Stripe or PayPal APIs
✅ Checkout page for collecting payment details
✅ Real-time payment status updates with Webhooks
✅ Cloudinary integration for image and invoice uploads
✅ Order creation and verification in MongoDB
✅ Invoice/receipt generation after successful payment
✅ Responsive UI built with Next.js
✅ Environment-based configuration for security

---

## ⚙️ Tech Stack

| Layer            | Technology                        |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------- |
| **Frontend**     | Next.js (React + API routes)      |
| **Backend**      | Node.js + Express.js              |
| **Database**     | MongoDB (Mongoose)                |
| **Payment API**  | Stripe / PayPal SDK               |
| **File Storage** | Cloudinary                        |
| **Optional**     | Nodemailer (for sending receipts) |

---

## 📁 Folder Structure

```
payment-gateway-project/
 ├── frontend/                 # Next.js frontend
 │   ├── pages/                # Pages (home, checkout, success, cancel)
 │   ├── components/           # UI components
 │   ├── lib/                  # API helper (Axios config)
 │   ├── styles/               # CSS files
 │   └── .env.local            # Frontend environment variables
 │
 └── backend/                  # Express.js backend
     ├── src/
     │   ├── config/           # DB, Stripe, Cloudinary setup
     │   ├── models/           # Product & Order schemas
     │   ├── routes/           # API routes
     │   ├── controllers/      # Logic for routes
     │   ├── webhooks/         # Stripe webhook handler
     │   ├── utils/            # Helper functions (invoice, email)
     │   ├── app.js            # Express setup
     │   └── server.js         # Server entry point
     └── .env                  # Backend environment variables
```

---

## 🔐 Environment Variables

### Frontend (`.env.local`)

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_1234
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5000
```

---

## 🛠️ Installation Steps

### 1️⃣ Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/saisarayu/payment-gateway.git
cd payment-gateway-project
```

### 2️⃣ Install dependencies

**Frontend**

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
```

**Backend**

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

### 3️⃣ Run the development servers

**Backend**

```bash
npm run dev
```

**Frontend**

```bash
npm run dev
```

* Frontend → [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
* Backend → [http://localhost:5000](http://localhost:5000)

---

## 💳 Payment Flow

1️⃣ User selects a product on the frontend.
2️⃣ Clicks “Pay Now” → Backend creates a **payment session** (Stripe/PayPal).
3️⃣ User completes payment securely on the gateway page.
4️⃣ Gateway redirects to `/success` or `/cancel`.
5️⃣ Webhook updates payment status in MongoDB.
6️⃣ Invoice generated and uploaded to **Cloudinary**.
7️⃣ Optional: Email invoice link to user.

---

## ☁️ Cloudinary Integration

Cloudinary is used for:

* Hosting **product images** (to display in frontend)
* Storing **generated invoices or receipts**

You can upload files using Cloudinary’s REST API or Node.js SDK.

